# Competency question (HEADLINE GATE): which slices assert a documentation-maturity
# tier their coverage does NOT support? The asserted ⊄ earned containment, expressed
# by INTENT INCLUSION — no rank predicate needed: a slice violates iff some dimension
# its CLAIMED anchor (gmeow:sliceDocMaturity) requires (gmeow:maturityRequiresDimension)
# is NOT among the dimensions the slice's documentation record COVERS
# (gmeow:docCoversDimension). Because the anchor intents nest (Minimal ⊆ Basic ⊆ Full
# ⊆ Maximal), "some required dimension is uncovered" is exactly "asserted's intent ⊄
# covered", which is exactly "earned's rank < asserted's rank". The claim is asserted
# on the real slice IRI (its manifest); the covered incidence is on the
# gmeow:DocumentedSlice record, so the query bridges the two via gmeow:documents —
# faithful to how crates/docs projects graph/documentation over the real slice graph.
# MUST return empty over the projected graph: no slice may claim beyond its coverage.
# Asserted lane; the anchor intents live in the module base graph.

PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>

SELECT ?slice WHERE {
    ?record a gmeow:DocumentedSlice ;
        gmeow:documents ?slice .
    ?slice gmeow:sliceDocMaturity ?anchor .
    ?anchor gmeow:maturityRequiresDimension ?dim .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?record gmeow:docCoversDimension ?dim }
}
ORDER BY ?slice
